# Copy to .env.local and edit. .env.local is gitignored; this file is not.
#
# Both are read at BUILD time by Next (NEXT_PUBLIC_* is inlined into the client
# bundle), so restart `npm run dev` after changing them — a page reload is not
# enough. If you leave them unset entirely, lib/config.ts falls back to
# 127.0.0.1:8000, which is right for a ctl running on this same machine.

# --- Local: ctl running on your own machine -------------------------------
#   uv run uvicorn ctl.main:app --port 8000
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000/api
NEXT_PUBLIC_FEED_URL=ws://127.0.0.1:8000/feed

# --- The agent, for the /agent page ---------------------------------------
# A SEPARATE process from ctl, on its own port:
#   uv run uvicorn agent.service:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8100
# It is not under /api — that prefix belongs to the control plane. The agent in
# turn needs a llama-server head started WITH --jinja; the /agent page header
# shows which head and which ctl it is actually using, so look there first when
# a question comes back as an error.
NEXT_PUBLIC_AGENT_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8100

# --- Cluster: ctl on the fabric -------------------------------------------
# 192.168.50.1 is where ctl answered during the Aug 22 bring-up. Only useful
# from a machine actually on that LAN; start ctl with `--host 0.0.0.0` or
# nothing off that box can reach it. Prefer the IP over `gpu-01` unless mDNS
# resolves from whichever laptop runs the browser.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://192.168.50.1:8000/api
# NEXT_PUBLIC_FEED_URL=ws://192.168.50.1:8000/feed
# NEXT_PUBLIC_AGENT_URL=http://192.168.50.1:8100

# Three things to get right:
#   1. The API base MUST end in /api. ctl serves REST at /api/nodes but mounts
#      the socket at bare /feed. Omit /api and every REST call 404s while the
#      WebSocket still works — a confusing half-broken state.
#   2. Feed is ws:// (or wss://), API is http:// (or https://). Different
#      schemes, easy to copy-paste wrong.
#   3. Both must point at the SAME host, or topology and job detail disagree.
